[W16-05] 6 is the unique perfect semiprime
Grade: 🟩
Uniqueness: Proven: even perfect = 2^(p-1)*(2^p-1); only p=2 gives semiprime. Unique.

Details:
  Semiprime = product of exactly 2 primes (counted with multiplicity)
  6 = 2*3: semiprime? True
  28 = 2^2*7: semiprime? False
  496: semiprime? False
  Perfect numbers <= 10000: [6, 28, 496, 8128]
  Perfect AND semiprime: [6]
  Even perfect numbers have form 2^(p-1)*(2^p-1).
  For p=2: 6=2*3 => 2 prime factors => semiprime!
  For p=3: 28=4*7 => 3 prime factors => not semiprime.
  => 6 is THE UNIQUE perfect semiprime.

