[W16-21] Nyquist(6 Hz) = 2*6 = 12 = sigma(6): holds IFF n is perfect
Grade: ⚪
Uniqueness: Holds for all perfect numbers. Not unique to 6.

Details:
  Nyquist sampling theorem: sample at >= 2f for signal at freq f.
  For f=6 Hz: Nyquist rate = 2*6 = 12 = sigma(6)
  For f=10: 2*10=20, sigma(10)=18. NOT equal.
  For f=12: 2*12=24, sigma(12)=28. NOT equal.
  For f=28: 2*28=56, sigma(28)=56. EQUAL! (28 is also perfect)
  Nyquist rate = 2n = sigma(n) IFF n is perfect.
  => This is equivalent to: n is perfect. Holds for all perfect n, not unique to 6.

