Details:
  Shannon sampling: bandwidth W, Nyquist rate = 2W.
  If W = n/phi(n) = 6/2 = 3, then 2W = 6 = n.
  This is tautological: 2*(n/phi(n))=n iff phi(n)=2, same as H23.
  Holds for n=3,4,6 (all with phi(n)=2).
  Not unique to 6.

